+      "text": "User instructions Manage user accounts Home is personal: your shift, work, assigned actions and recorded contributions. The complete permission-filtered card directory is on Workspaces, directly below Home in the sidebar. Direct module links remain. Open and Create have different purposes; the familiar task-type card chooser is retained. Access for the right people; attribution stays with their work Open Admin → Users & access . Add a named account for each person and assign Technician, Supervisor or Administrator access. Department membership controls eligible item approvals; it does not grant administrator access. New and reset passwords must contain 6–128 characters . The same minimum applies when a user changes their own password. Existing passwords continue to work without being reset. Prefer a longer unique passphrase and follow your organisation’s account policy. Who can open the Admin console? Any enabled Administrator account on the same hub can sign in. It does not have to be the first administrator. An account from a different hub will not give access. A deleted or disabled account cannot sign in. Remove or restore an account Action Result Delete user… Removes the account from Current users and immediately blocks hub access. Saved checks, approvals and history remain attributed to the same person. Restore user… Select Deleted users, restore the account and review it. It returns Disabled; use Edit / disable to enable it deliberately. Delete permanently… Available for an unused deleted account only. Existing checklist, approval or history references block permanent removal. Earlier backups and the account-management audit remain. Deletion requires the exact User ID and a reason. You cannot delete your signed-in account. At least one enabled administrator must remain. Before removing access, ask the person to synchronise or export any unsent work. Deletion does not remove required approvals. Arrange an eligible replacement reviewer or restore the account when necessary; do not clear the phone’s saved work. Accounts belong to the selected project. Setup-only profile imports create disabled Technicians: assign a password and reviewed role before enabling them. Full-project transfers retain imported administrator credentials. Per-user operational access Select a user in Users & access and choose Permissions… to control viewing, entry, correction and other actions. Read Set user permissions for the available choices. Administrators keep full access; restricted users use Technician or Supervisor roles. For a person who must see only selected vessels, use Fleet & manifests → User vessel access and explicitly choose Vessel-only access. General project permissions and department membership are not vessel boundaries. Read Set vessel-only access before changing an account. Invite a verified member without granting role defaults Use Invitations & access for mailbox-verified onboarding, pending/deny-all accounts and scoped approval. Existing manually created local accounts retain their established role defaults; the older Create user action is a deliberate administrator-created operational account, not an invitation. Existing IDs and authorship are never automatically merged by matching email or name. Invited people choose a User ID and can check their own status at /join-team. Email-only main sign-in and domain registration are not enabled here. Read the complete invitation and approval workflow . HR and your private staff records Open HR from People, or My HR records on your own profile. My records shows the documents, travel, crew assignments, timesheets and expenses belonging to your named account in the current company. Staff selection appears only with an HR management or review permission. Each permission controls its own area; travel access does not reveal another employee’s passport or expenses. Staff documents are kept in HR rather than the equipment Certificates register or public Team profile. Enable employee and HR access A company administrator uses the existing account Permissions editor to grant HR: view own records and the appropriate document, timesheet or expense submission rights to employees. Grant document management, travel management, crew assignment management and timesheet/expense review separately to authorised HR staff. These management rights cover the company and are not inferred from Supervisor or department-head titles. Existing explicit permission settings remain explicit: new HR rights must be granted when absent. Normal named employees using inherited role defaults can use their own HR submission rights. Pending, disabled, guest, access-code and vessel-only sessions cannot use HR. Certificates, passport and seaman’s book In Documents , add the document type and title, reference, issuer and source dates. Passport, Seaman’s book, Medical, Training, Visa/work permit and Other are available. Choose a recorded expiry date, explicitly no expiry or unknown expiry. A blank date remains unknown. Set the reminder window in days; 90 days is the starting value. Due soon and Expired are derived from the recorded expiry date in UTC. They do not authenticate the document or confirm eligibility for travel or work. Save the record, then attach the source PDF, PNG or JPEG. The limit is 5 MiB per file and six active files per record. HR can add records to a selected person; employees with document submission rights can maintain their own. Opening a file uses the current HR access check. Archive hides current reminders while retaining the record and history. A renewed document can be a new record; keep the earlier supplied evidence. Travel and dated crew assignments Authorised HR staff record a person’s travel origin, destination, dates and optional times with an explicit time zone, booking reference, accommodation and status. Saving details records arrangements; it does not book tickets. Crew assignments record joining/leaving dates, vessel or location, department and optional day/night shift window. Planned, Confirmed, Completed and Cancelled states are explicit. These dated HR assignments are separate from current department handover cycles; HR changes do not automatically rewrite a handover roster. Complete and review timesheets Create a timesheet for a period of up to 31 days. Add one line per date, hours, work location and activity such as offshore, onshore, travel, standby or leave. Hours are recorded to two decimal places, from zero to 24 per day. Save a draft while preparing it. Submit sends the exact saved entries for review. Submitted and approved entries are locked. An authorised reviewer can approve or return the sheet with a comment; the employee can correct a returned sheet and submit it again. Reviewers cannot approve their own submissions. Totals are recorded hours; Wavelink does not calculate payroll or overtime entitlement. Prepare expenses and receipts Enter the expense date, category, merchant, amount, currency, project and description. Save a draft, attach the receipt and then submit. Amounts use up to two decimal places and a three-letter currency code, such as BRL, USD or EUR. Totals stay separate for each currency; no exchange rate is inferred. The employee edits draft or returned claims only. Reviewers approve or return submitted claims, with a required comment for returns. No self-approval is allowed. Submitted and approved receipt attachments remain locked with the submitted claim. Expiry reminders and safe saves Your HR overview and the bell’s HR category show due/expired documents you are allowed to read. The existing Notification preferences control in-app categories and quiet hours. Optional HR email is off until you select it in your personal Email alerts settings, using a verified mailbox and a configured company mail service. Email contains category counts and a link; document references and files stay inside authorised HR pages. Save working records as drafts before leaving. An unfinished editor asks you to review the change before navigation or sign-out. A connection loss after sending offers Retry unchanged request , preserving the original action reference. Keep that form open while resolving an uncertain outcome; a retry does not duplicate committed work. Another person’s change produces a version conflict instead of silently overwriting it. This HR workspace needs a connection and does not save private document bytes into browser recovery storage. HR in backups and transfers Complete company backups containing HR records require administrator access and include sensitive staff documents, timesheets, expenses and history. Protect those unencrypted files. HR is unchecked by default in selected-module exports. Selecting other modules does not move private HR data into them or reset the existing company’s HR records. Opening an imported company uses the normal account and administrator-review safeguards.",
