+<details class="help-scope"><summary>About these instructions</summary><p>This reader standardises presentation, not the entire procedure library. The original instructions, version labels and warnings are retained. Some topics describe the local Windows hub or earlier interface labels. They must not be read as proof that all desktop setup, imports or recovery work is available in the hosted browser.</p><p>The full wording, hosted/local scope, native Help and PDF review remains on the development list. Use only company-approved operational procedures; viewing Help does not approve a checklist, release equipment or verify work.</p></details><details class="help-outline"><summary>On this page <span>9 sections</span></summary><ol><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-1">Find the record or its source</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-2">Add or edit a register record</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-3">Dates and unknown expiry</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-4">Attach and read sources</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-5">Prepare and activate a replacement</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-6">Drafts, retries and changing accounts</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-7">Refresh without losing the view</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-section-8">Reports and boundaries</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#local-module-forms">This section’s local forms</a></li></ol></details><article><p class="eyebrow">CERTIFICATES · REGISTER AND SOURCE FILES</p><h1>Certificates</h1><p id="hr-personal-documents">For employee certificates, passports and seaman’s books, open HR from People or My HR records. These private staff documents have separate access from this equipment register. <a href="/help/topics/users#hr-workspace">Read the HR guide</a></p>
 <p>A certificate record describes supplied source information. Wavelink does not issue, authenticate or sign the original certificate and does not approve equipment for use. Draft is a register state, not a private personal draft.</p>
 <h2 id="help-section-1">Find the record or its source</h2><p>Open <strong>Certificates</strong>. Use <strong>Current revisions, Due soon, Expired, Drafts, Archived / superseded or All revisions</strong>, then search by title, number, issuer or equipment. <strong>Responsible contact</strong> can filter by a returned named person or department, by your own named contact identity, or no recorded contact. This does not create a Task, grant access, or make a private audience. <strong>Reset filters</strong> restores the current register. Same-account refresh preserves your choices; another account/project resets them.</p>
 <p>Cards show expiry, contact and source-file count. Select a card to open the full record. <strong>Source files</strong> jumps directly to its attachments; dates, scope/conditions, notes, equipment and revision links remain in the same record. <strong>History</strong> reads the actual saved changes. <strong>Record PDF</strong> exports this revision's register report, not an original issued certificate.</p>
